  "difficulty_reason": "After the named Kunz-face correspondence, basic finite-monoid factorization and Farkas prerequisites are supplied, the necessary new local core proves faithful min-plus recovery of every factorization from projected face weights, constructs the pure Kunz fan, and identifies its projected cones with all Betti equalities and inequalities through terminating reduction. These ingredients then force a unique inner trade on every interior codimension1 face, unique endpoint factorizations of each element and a global two-sided choice for every incident staircase chamber. The H proposal concerns this complete factorization-to-face realization and chamber incidence mechanism; unrelated later Groebner-fan, enumeration and extremal-presentation applications are not used to raise difficulty, and final residual qualification is left to independent root review.",
